  "question": {
    "text": "The number of carbonyl carbon in the product <math> <mtext>X</mtext> </math> is<br />\r<math> <mrow> <mtext>Propyne</mtext><munderover> <mo>→</mo> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>Zn/H</mtext></mrow> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <mtext>O</mtext></mrow> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>/CH</mtext></mrow> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>Cl</mtext></mrow> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <mtext>,Δ</mtext></mrow> </munderover> <mtext>X</mtext></mrow> </math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Ozonolysis of propyne results in the formation of <math><mn>2</mn></math> -oxopropanal which contains keto group and aldehyde <math><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>)</mo></math> group. Hence, <math><mn>2</mn></math> -oxopropanal contains two carbon atoms. <br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/98b3c698-f388-4e7c-97a0-b67f3b2d9d6a.png\" style=\"width:5.09375in;height:1.34653in\">",
